{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/966907-what-attribute-and-skill-for-using-a-drone","id":966907,"title":"What Attribute and Skill for Using a drone ?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-10T13:49:43-07:00","id":966907,"title":"What Attribute and Skill for Using a drone ?","content":"Being Drones are pretty easy to get today. I wanted to know what kind of dice roll someone should do to use a drone to take a photo of an area or fly through a building.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T14:05:11-07:00","id":966914,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure Hurt Locker has an entire Style Merit for drone piloting, which would indicate that it will have all of the relevant gameplay information.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T15:21:24-07:00","id":966948,"title":"","content":"It depends. Probably Wits + Computer or Drive (since it even covers helicopters) - Drone Handling - Environmental Penalties","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T15:21:26-07:00","id":966949,"title":"","content":"I'd probably have smaller civilian drones be Computers, and larger industrial/scientific/military drones be Drive (with appropriate specialty). The more complex the drone, the more operating it becomes like operating the real thing.<br /> <br /> Attributes are more situational. Complex maneuvers = really good hand-eye coordination = Dex. Sudden maneuvers = Wits. Generally flying probably = Intelligence. Flying for long periods of time = Resolve or Stamina.<br /> <br /> At least until Hurt Locker drops as noted above.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T18:30:55-07:00","id":971056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/966907-what-attribute-and-skill-for-using-a-drone?p=966948#post966948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It depends. Probably Wits + Computer or Drive (since it even covers helicopters) - Drone Handling - Environmental Penalties</div> </div> </div> </div> Why is handling a penalty there? It's always been like the drive equipment bonus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T01:13:49-07:00","id":971199,"title":"","content":"I'd assume because remote piloting is inherently more difficult than direct piloting, it would be safe to say that most drones will have a negative to zero Handling rating rather than a positive one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T03:23:58-07:00","id":971235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/966907-what-attribute-and-skill-for-using-a-drone?p=971056#post971056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why is handling a penalty there? It's always been like the drive equipment bonus.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It was the case in 1E if I remember correctly. Now it's almost always a penalty (unless you have a modified and/or expensive vehicle).<br /> Look at the Vehicles section in CofD core rulebook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}